.TH RPILEDCONFIG 8 2026-11-11 "rpiledconfig" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
rpiledconfig \- WiFi setup for a Raspberry Pi over Bluetooth, keyed by its LED
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rpiledconfig
.RB [ \-c
.IR path ]
.br
.B rpiledconfig
.B \-\-print\-vectors
.br
.B rpiledconfig
.RB \-v | \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rpiledconfig
advertises a Bluetooth LE service through BlueZ.
When the RPi LED Config app asks, it draws a one-time 64-bit key
and blinks it on the Pi's activity LED for the phone's camera to read.
The phone proves it holds the key with SPAKE2,
and everything after is encrypted with AES-GCM.
The app can then list the networks the Pi sees and hand one to NetworkManager,
and can remove the service from the Pi.
.PP
It is started by systemd as
.BR rpiledconfig.service ,
runs as the unprivileged user
.BR rpiledconfig ,
and stops cleanly on SIGTERM, giving the LED back its trigger.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIpath\fR"
Read the configuration from
.IR path .
.TP
.B \-\-print\-vectors
Print the protocol's test vectors and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a summary of the options and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RPILEDCONFIG_CONFIG
The configuration to read when
.B \-\-config
is not given.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/rpiledconfig/rpiledconfig.conf
The configuration, read when neither
.B \-\-config
nor
.B RPILEDCONFIG_CONFIG
is given. Every setting is described in
.IR /usr/share/doc/rpiledconfig/configuration.md .
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/rpiledconfig/
The protocol, the security notes, installation and configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR bluetoothctl (1),
.BR nmcli (1)
.PP
https://github.com/tomdionysus/rpiledconfig
